From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] catch2: allocate the alternate signal stack at runtime

License: BSL-1.0
Upstream-Status: downstream adaptation
Origin: https://github.com/catchorg/Catch2/commit/8f277a54c0b9c1d1024dedcb2dec1d206971e745

Modern glibc exposes signal stack sizes through sysconf, so they cannot
size a constexpr array. Adapt the upstream runtime allocation approach
to this older bundled Catch2 without replacing its reporting interfaces.
Keep the signal handlers and allocate their alternate stack once, using
the larger of 32 KiB and SIGSTKSZ as in upstream's fix. The vector owns
the stable storage for the process lifetime; no test or signal handler
resizes it, and it is automatically released during static destruction.

Remove when the bundled Catch2 supports runtime signal stack sizes.

--- a/lib/catch2/catch.hpp
+++ b/lib/catch2/catch.hpp
@@ -7945,3 +7945,3 @@
         static stack_t oldSigStack;
-        static char altStackMem[];
+        static std::vector<char> altStackMem;

@@ -10716,3 +10716,3 @@
     // is experimentally determined, so that's not guaranteed.
-    static constexpr std::size_t sigStackSize = 32768 >= MINSIGSTKSZ ? 32768 : MINSIGSTKSZ;
+    static const std::size_t sigStackSize = 32768 >= SIGSTKSZ ? 32768 : SIGSTKSZ;

@@ -10742,5 +10742,5 @@
         isSet = true;
         stack_t sigStack;
-        sigStack.ss_sp = altStackMem;
+        sigStack.ss_sp = altStackMem.data();
         sigStack.ss_size = sigStackSize;
         sigStack.ss_flags = 0;
@@ -10775,3 +10775,3 @@
     stack_t FatalConditionHandler::oldSigStack = {};
-    char FatalConditionHandler::altStackMem[sigStackSize] = {};
+    std::vector<char> FatalConditionHandler::altStackMem(sigStackSize);
